review.reviewBody:
I enjoyed sourcing ingredients and making this. I did make substitutions (just for convenience and to use what I had):
1) ~1tbsp of chili oil and 2 red thai chilies for the pickled chilies;
2) chopped, unsalted, roasted peanuts for the mince;
3) indian eggplants for chinese eggplants;
4) honey for sugar.
On the whole, I thought it was nice, but a tad too vinegary—I suspect the meat would offset that, so I might try this again with meat—although the peanuts offered great texture, so I might do both! Interestingly, I also found I needed a dash of salt and, once I did that, it actually offset the vinegar a bit. I'm also going to get the chinese eggplants next time, though the baby ones were not bad.
